/target
/out
/client/Binaries
/client/Intermediate
/client/Saved
/client/DerivedDataCache
/client/.vs
/client/Plugins/McpAutomationBridge/Binaries
/client/Plugins/McpAutomationBridge/Intermediate

# Surface textures and the archives they come from. They live outside
# client/Content on purpose: Content is for cooked .uasset, and loose
# source files under it are a directory the editor watches and reimports. Roughly 80 MB a set, and a
# gigabyte across the biome list — none of it authored here, all of it
# re-fetchable from the asset ids the manifest records. That is what the
# manifest is for. manifest.json itself is committed: it is the provenance, and
# losing it is the thing that cannot be undone.
/incoming
/surfaces/*/

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Imported texture assets and build intermediates. Both are derived: the
# .uasset come from surfaces/ via tools/make_import_settings.py and Unreal's
# ImportAssets commandlet, and surfaces/ comes from the Fab vault. Everything
# needed to rebuild them is committed; 2.3 GB of derived binaries is not.
/client/Content/Surfaces
/build
